<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i+1));</code>

This assert statement captures the condition that if the index is within the valid range (from 0 to the size of the list inclusive) and the role is not null, then for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at the next position in the old list is either null if the old element was null or equals the old element at that position.
