<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i-1)) == null ? null : \old(this.get(i-1)));</code>

However, the above assertion seems to have a logical error. The correct assertion should ensure that the element at the current index `i` is equal to the element at the previous index `i-1` from the old list, shifted up by one position due to the insertion. Here's the corrected version:

<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index < i && i <= \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1));</code>

This ensures that starting from the insertion point `index`, each element in the new list is equal to the element at the previous position in the old list.
