<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i-1)) == null ? null : \old(this.get(i-1)));</code>

However, the above assertion seems incorrect based on the intended meaning of the comment. Let's correct it:

The comment suggests that for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null if the old element was null or equals the old element at that position. This means the element at position `i` should be equal to the element at position `i-1` before the insertion.

Here is the corrected assert statement:

<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index < i && i <= \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1));</code>

This ensures that starting from the index after the insertion point, each element is equal to the element at the previous position before the insertion.
